# Environment

- {world}
- **Working directory:** `{workspace}`, a git repository; this file is `{workspace}/AGENTS.md`. Only `{workspace}`
  and `/tmp` are writable.
- **Pythons** (nothing can be installed; `PYTHONPATH` is `{code}`, so each can `import robot`[[ and `import vision`]]):
  - `{robot_python}` (first on `PATH`, as `python`): numpy, scipy, mujoco, mink, ruckig, warp, i2rt, pillow.
  - `{perception_python}`: numpy, scipy, opencv, torch, jax, matplotlib, transformers, pillow.
  - `{libs_python}`: numpy, scipy, cuRobo, PyRoKi (with jax, jaxls, yourdfpy), trimesh, torch, warp, matplotlib,
    pillow.
  - None of them has Pinocchio or Open3D.
- {gpu}
- **Memory:** a process that uses more than {mem_process_gb} GB of RAM is killed at once, and so is the largest of
  yours when all of them together use more than {mem_total_gb} GB.{commands}
- **No internet:** your programs can connect only to the robot socket[[ and the vision socket]]. No other network is
  reachable, whatever the sandbox settings say.
- **The robot:** `import robot; r = robot.connect()` connects through `$ROBOT_ADDR` (`{robot_addr}`). Every file
  `r.description` names (URDFs, the MJCF and their meshes) is readable.
[[- **Vision:** `import vision; v = vision.connect()` connects through `$VISION_ADDR` (`{vision_addr}`) to perception
  models running on a GPU in another process. Its manual is `{code}/docs/VISION.md`.
]]- **Code:** `{code}`, read-only: `robot/` (the robot client), `robotd/core/` (the driver's control core)[[,
  `vision/` (the vision client)]] and `docs/` (`MANUAL.md` is the robot manual, copied below[[; `VISION.md` the vision
  manual]]).{examples}
- **Time:** {wall_h} hours of wall-clock time from the start of the episode ({started}); `date` gives the time. At the
  limit the episode ends wherever things are.
- **Ending:** call `r.finish(summary)` when you are done, then stop. The episode ends when you stop or at the time
  limit. Nobody answers questions during the episode, and no success signal comes back.

